{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.124.1.a001", "note": "Construct noun takes its own word; supplied indefinite article joins the noun under rule 15.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a002", "note": "Article on the rectum; ASV writes no 'the' for the phrase (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.002", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a003", "note": "Rectum takes the chain's 'of' (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a004", "note": "Authorship lamed rendered 'of'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a006", "note": "לוּלֵי 'if not' takes the discontinuous 'If ... not' (rule 25). Competing reading: fold the whole 'If it had not been' into the particle as a fixed formula under rule 30; I kept the copula with the predicate under rule 20 and left the cleft dummy added.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t010"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a007", "note": "Cleft/impersonal 'it' in a verbless clause; no morpheme licenses it (rule 20).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a008", "note": "Jehovah is the predicate of the verbless לוּלֵי clause and takes the construction-supplied copula 'had been' (rule 20), discontinuous around 'not'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a009", "note": "Written relative takes 'who'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a011", "note": "לְ 'for us' recast as 'on our side'; the fixed phrase belongs to the preposition, discontinuous around the suffix's 'our', headed on the content word 'side' (rule 24).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a012", "note": "Suffix takes the possessive the recasting writes for it (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a013", "note": "Jussive takes the volitive frame 'Let ... say' (rule 17), discontinuous around subject and particle.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a014", "note": "נָא rendered 'now'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "PSA.124.1.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.124.1.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.124.1.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}], "ref": "PSA.124.1", "review_notes": ["Verbless לוּלֵי clause with a written relative: 'If ... not' to the particle, copula to the predicate name, cleft 'it' added, 'who' to שֶׁ."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
